<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Almenar (1082)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1082">1082</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Almenar was fought in 1082 near Almenar, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> in Catalonia. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, commanding for al-Mutaman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, defeated an alliance of al-Mutaman's brother al-Mundhir of Lleida, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a> with Count Berenguer Ramon II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, whom he captured. The victory strengthened Zaragoza and the Cid's reputation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-almenar-1082.jpg" alt="Battle of Almenar (1082)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deosringas · CC BY-SA 3.0 es · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castell_d%27Almenar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
